      "message": "How about making `trng_rnd64` return `[u64; 3]` rather than `(u64, u64, u64)`, and then use `zerocopy::AsBytes` to do something like:\n\n```rust\nlet result \u003d trng_rnd64(...)?;\nchunk.copy_from_slice(\u0026result.as_bytes()[..chunk.len()]);\n```\n\nYou\u0027re already assuming native byte order, so I think that\u0027s equivalent?",
